{"id": "9c5c3da4-5103-4d91-8447-0b394f3c13c5", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check ECR repositories' lifecycle policies against images currently in use by running workloads (ECS, EKS, Lambda) in this account/region.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_Lw3VgERr0TWD1jyMK47qYW", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "For every ECR repository in this AWS account in us-east-1, determine whether the repository's lifecycle policy would expire/delete any image tag or digest that is currently in use by a running workload. Summarize per repository.",
  "context": "User wants to know if any ECR lifecycle policy rule is at risk of deleting an image that's actively running, before it causes an outage. Need to correlate ECR repo images (tags, digests, push dates) and lifecycle policy rules against what's actually deployed/running right now.",
  "resources": [
    "All ECR repositories in account 012345678901_1, region us-east-1",
    "ECS clusters/services/task definitions (container image references) in us-east-1",
    "EKS clusters and running pod images in us-east-1 (if any EKS clusters exist)",
    "Lambda functions using container image package type in us-east-1 (if any)"
  ],
  "timeframe": "current state as of now",
  "criteria": "For each ECR repo: 1) fetch the lifecycle policy (if any) and understand its rules (e.g. expire untagged after N days, keep only N most recent images matching a tag pattern, etc). 2) List images in the repo with tags/digests and pushedAt dates. 3) Determine which images are currently referenced by running ECS tasks/services, EKS pods, or Lambda functions. 4) Evaluate whether the lifecycle policy's rules would currently select (and thus eventually delete) any image that is on the 'currently running' list. Flag repos where there's a real conflict (policy would delete a running image) vs repos with no lifecycle policy, no running images from that repo, or policies that clearly exclude the running image's tag. Summarize per repository: policy summary, running image(s), at-risk or not, and why."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Cross-reference ECR lifecycle policies with running images in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

